window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-24d888be8e5fa72d"]={"zh":"<h1 id=\"codex-cli\">Codex CLI</h1> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code> 可获取对应 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"inspect-edit-and-run-code-from-your-terminal\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">在终端中检查、编辑并运行代码</h2> <p>Codex CLI 是通过命令行界面（CLI）使用 Codex 的方式：无需离开终端，即可检查代码、进行修改、运行命令，并自动化可重复的工作。</p> <p><a id=\"start-here\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_2\">从这里开始</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d?anchor=getting-started\">安装 Codex</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">CLI 命令参考</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"why-use-codex-cli\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"codex-cli_1\">为什么使用 Codex CLI</h3> <ul> <li><strong>直接处理本地代码库：</strong> 让 Codex 检查文件、进行编辑，并运行计算机上已经安装的工具。</li> <li><strong>由你掌控：</strong> 根据任务选择模型、推理强度、权限和命令。</li> <li><strong>与脚本和 CI（持续集成）配合：</strong> 既可以交互式使用 Codex，也可以在可重复执行的工作流和流水线中调用 codex exec。</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"_3\">开始使用</h2> <p><a id=\"getting-started\"></a></p> <p><strong>开始使用 Codex CLI。</strong></p> <p>安装 Codex、登录，然后在项目目录中运行第一个任务。</p> <p><a id=\"1-install-codex\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"1-codex\">1. 安装 Codex</h3> <p>选择以下一种安装方式：</p> <h4 id=\"macoslinux\">macOS/Linux</h4> <p>使用适用于 macOS 和 Linux 的独立安装程序安装 Codex CLI。</p> <p><strong>安装：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh\n</code></pre> <p><strong>更新：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"windows\">Windows</h4> <p>使用适用于 Windows 的独立安装程序安装 Codex CLI。</p> <p>请在新的 PowerShell 窗口中运行以下命令。</p> <p><strong>安装：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c \"irm https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1 | iex\"\n</code></pre> <p><strong>更新：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c \"irm https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1 | iex\"\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"npm\">npm</h4> <p>也可以使用 npm 安装 Codex CLI。</p> <p><strong>安装：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install -g @openai/codex\n</code></pre> <p><strong>更新：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install -g @openai/codex\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"homebrew\">Homebrew</h4> <p>也可以使用 Homebrew 安装 Codex CLI。</p> <p><strong>安装：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">brew install --cask codex\n</code></pre> <p><strong>更新：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">brew upgrade --cask codex\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"2-run-codex-and-sign-in\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"2-codex\">2. 运行 Codex 并登录</h3> <p>打开一个项目目录并运行 <code>codex</code>。首次运行 Codex 时，请选择<strong>使用 ChatGPT 登录</strong>或其他可用的登录方式。</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">查看身份验证选项</a></p> <p><a id=\"3-start-your-first-task\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"3\">3. 开始第一个任务</h3> <p>描述你希望完成的工作。例如，可以让 Codex 介绍项目、进行范围明确的修改，或帮助调试问题。</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Tell me about this project\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">向我介绍这个项目。</div></div> <p>在任务开始前和结束后创建 Git 检查点，以便需要时还原更改。请参阅<a href=\"#/article/a-67a7ce1fea36da0d\">最佳实践（官方来源暂不可用）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"next-steps\"></a></p> <h3 id=\"_4\">接下来</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">探索 CLI 命令参考</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f05fc21d24fe24c1\">配置 Codex</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">使用 codex exec 实现自动化</a></li> </ul> <p><a id=\"see-what-codex-cli-can-do\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cli_2\">了解 Codex CLI 能做什么</h2> <p>通过一个专注的终端工作循环，完成交互式操作、自动化、代码审查和任务委派。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">在终端中完成编码循环</a>：在代码库中启动 Codex，了解陌生代码、规划更改、编辑文件，并运行本地开发工具。你可以在当前轮次中调整方向、查看执行中的命令和差异，并在同一会话中继续跟进。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">使用技能和插件</a>：将可重复使用的指令打包为技能，再添加插件，以便在 CLI 中连接团队的工具和数据。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">在发布前审查更改</a>：针对未提交的更改、某个提交或基准分支运行专门的审查。Codex 会报告按优先级排序的问题，但不会修改工作树，让你能在提交或创建拉取请求前处理风险。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"build-a-terminal-workflow-around-codex\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex\">围绕 Codex 构建终端工作流</h2> <p>了解 CLI 中可用于恢复会话、补充视觉和网页上下文、拆分复杂任务以及连接开发工具的功能。</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=codex-resume\"><strong>返回已保存的聊天</strong></a> — <code>codex resume</code>：重新打开当前代码库中的最近聊天；需要查找更早的工作时，也可以搜索本地聊天记录。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\"><strong>在提示中加入视觉上下文</strong></a> — <code>codex --image</code>：在首次提示中附上错误截图、架构图或设计参考，也可以把图片粘贴到交互式输入框中。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\"><strong>拆分较大的调查任务</strong></a> — <code>subagents</code>：让 Codex 把范围明确的工作交给专门的子智能体处理，再将发现汇总回主终端会话。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\"><strong>搜索当前信息</strong></a> — <code>codex --search</code>：当任务依赖最新版本、文档或外部行为时，切换为实时网页搜索。搜索过程会显示在对话记录中。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad?sectionMissing=use-codex-cloud-from-the-cli\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\"><strong>将工作交给 Codex 云端</strong>（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a> — <code>codex cloud</code>：查看正在进行和已完成的聊天，将工作提交到已配置的环境，并从终端把结果应用到本地代码库。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\"><strong>通过 MCP 连接外部工具</strong></a> — <code>codex mcp</code>：添加本地或远程 MCP 服务器；如有需要可进行身份验证，并在使用前检查当前会话可用的工具。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\"><strong>设置每次运行的权限边界</strong></a> — <code>/permissions</code>：选择 Codex 何时可以不询问就编辑文件或运行命令；继续操作前，也可以查看当前生效的沙箱和可写根目录。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2a01a9d34cde2424\"><strong>让 Codex 适配你的终端</strong></a> — <code>codex completion</code>：为 Shell 生成自动补全、选择语法主题，并在 VISUAL 或 EDITOR 指定的编辑器中撰写较长提示。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"use-codex-cli-when\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"codex-cli_3\">适合使用 Codex CLI 的情况</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">你主要在终端中工作</a>：在同一个专注的工作循环中浏览、编辑和运行代码库。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">你需要脚本或 CI 自动化</a>：在可重复执行的工作流中运行非交互式命令。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">你希望在本地进行代码审查</a>：在提交或创建拉取请求前检查更改。</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad?sectionMissing=use-codex-cloud-from-the-cli\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">你希望把工作交给云端（官网章节，需联网）</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">本地页面（未识别该章节）</a>：启动云端聊天，稍后再回到终端继续。</li> </ul>","en":"<h1 id=\"codex-cli\">Codex CLI</h1> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"inspect-edit-and-run-code-from-your-terminal\">Inspect, edit, and run code from your terminal</h2> <p>Inspect code, make changes, run commands, and automate repeatable work without leaving your terminal.</p> <h3 id=\"start-here\">Start here</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-24d888be8e5fa72d?anchor=getting-started\">Install Codex</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">CLI reference</a></li> </ul> <h3 id=\"why-use-codex-cli\">Why use Codex CLI</h3> <ul> <li><strong>Work against your local repository:</strong> Let Codex inspect files, make edits, and run the tools already installed on your machine.</li> <li><strong>Stay in control:</strong> Choose the model, reasoning effort, permissions, and commands that fit the task.</li> <li><strong>Compose with scripts and CI:</strong> Use Codex interactively or call codex exec from repeatable workflows and pipelines.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"getting-started\">Getting started</h2> <p><strong>Get started with Codex CLI.</strong></p> <p>Install Codex, sign in, and run your first task from a project directory.</p> <h3 id=\"1-install-codex\">1. Install Codex</h3> <p>Choose one of these install methods:</p> <h4 id=\"macoslinux\">macOS/Linux</h4> <p>Install the Codex CLI with the standalone installer for macOS and Linux.</p> <p><strong>Install:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Update:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">curl -fsSL https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.sh | sh\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"windows\">Windows</h4> <p>Install the Codex CLI with the standalone installer for Windows. Start these from a new PowerShell window.</p> <p><strong>Install:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c \"irm https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1 | iex\"\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Update:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-powershell\">powershell -ExecutionPolicy ByPass -c \"irm https://chatgpt.com/codex/install.ps1 | iex\"\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"npm\">npm</h4> <p>You can also install the Codex CLI with npm.</p> <p><strong>Install:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install -g @openai/codex\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Update:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">npm install -g @openai/codex\n</code></pre> <h4 id=\"homebrew\">Homebrew</h4> <p>You can also install the Codex CLI with Homebrew.</p> <p><strong>Install:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">brew install --cask codex\n</code></pre> <p><strong>Update:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-bash\">brew upgrade --cask codex\n</code></pre> <h3 id=\"2-run-codex-and-sign-in\">2. Run Codex and sign in</h3> <p>Open a project directory and run <code>codex</code>. The first time you run Codex, choose <strong>Sign in with ChatGPT</strong> or another available sign-in method.</p> <p><a href=\"#/article/a-1454a3aad1fa2115\">Review authentication options</a></p> <h3 id=\"3-start-your-first-task\">3. Start your first task</h3> <p>Describe what you want to accomplish. For example, ask Codex to explain the project, make a focused change, or help debug an issue.</p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Tell me about this project\n</code></pre> <p>Create Git checkpoints before and after a task so you can revert changes. See the <a href=\"#/article/a-67a7ce1fea36da0d\">best practices (official source unavailable)</a>.</p> <h3 id=\"next-steps\">Next steps</h3> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Explore the CLI reference</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f05fc21d24fe24c1\">Configure Codex</a></li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">Automate with codex exec</a></li> </ul> <h2 id=\"see-what-codex-cli-can-do\">See what Codex CLI can do</h2> <p>Use one focused terminal loop for interactive work, automation, review, and delegation.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">Keep the coding loop in your terminal</a>: Start Codex in a repository to explore unfamiliar code, plan a change, edit files, and run your local development tools. Steer the active turn, inspect commands and diffs as they appear, and keep follow-up work in the same session.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-f06621b97709dae2\">Use skills and plugins</a>: Package repeatable instructions as skills, then add plugins to connect Codex to your team's tools and data without leaving the CLI.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">Review changes before they ship</a>: Run a dedicated review against uncommitted changes, a commit, or a base branch. Codex reports prioritized findings without modifying your working tree, so you can address risks before you commit or open a pull request.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"build-a-terminal-workflow-around-codex\">Build a terminal workflow around Codex</h2> <p>Learn about the CLI features you can use to resume sessions, add visual and web context, split up complex work, and connect Codex to your development tools.</p> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3?anchor=codex-resume\"><strong>Return to a saved chat</strong></a> — <code>codex resume</code>: Reopen a recent chat from the current repository, or search across local chats when you need to return to older work.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b64a9457088d1171\"><strong>Bring visual context into the prompt</strong></a> — <code>codex --image</code>: Pass an error screenshot, architecture diagram, or design reference with the first prompt, or paste an image into the interactive composer.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-731168d993ec5d2b\"><strong>Split up a larger investigation</strong></a> — <code>subagents</code>: Ask Codex to delegate focused work to specialized agents, then bring their findings back into the main terminal session.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-eb946260804133fb\"><strong>Search for current context</strong></a> — <code>codex --search</code>: Switch a run to live web search when a task depends on current releases, documentation, or external behavior. Search activity stays visible in the transcript.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad?sectionMissing=use-codex-cloud-from-the-cli\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\"><strong>Move work to Codex cloud</strong> (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Local page (section not recognized)</a> — <code>codex cloud</code>: Browse active and completed chats, submit work to a configured environment, and apply the result to your local repository from the terminal.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-dd3c07a3ae6aafeb\"><strong>Connect external tools with MCP</strong></a> — <code>codex mcp</code>: Add local or remote MCP servers, authenticate when needed, and inspect the tools available to the current session before Codex uses them.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-b7af4e0dbfe643b3\"><strong>Set the boundaries for each run</strong></a> — <code>/permissions</code>: Choose when Codex can edit files or run commands without asking, and inspect the active sandbox and writable roots before you continue.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-2a01a9d34cde2424\"><strong>Fit Codex to your terminal</strong></a> — <code>codex completion</code>: Generate completions for your shell, choose a syntax theme, and open longer prompts in the editor configured by VISUAL or EDITOR.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"use-codex-cli-when\">Use Codex CLI when…</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-820e54e1b31b71d3\">You work from the terminal</a>: Explore, edit, and run a repository in one focused loop.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-8e570f2a8916c65a\">You need scripting or CI</a>: Run a non-interactive command in a repeatable workflow.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-47b0440a51c2fc92\">You want a local code review</a>: Inspect changes before you commit or open a pull request.</li> <li><a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad?sectionMissing=use-codex-cloud-from-the-cli\" title=\"旧来源章节未在本地快照中定位，打开该文章；可通过官方来源查看当前章节。\">You want to hand work to the cloud (official section, online)</a> <a href=\"#/article/a-c302e8415c7f61ad\">Local page (section not recognized)</a>: Launch a cloud chat and return to the terminal later.</li> </ul>"};
